# REVIEWER_LANES.md

> Every automated review lane this repository has ever had, in effect or not.
> A lane is a **lane, not an authority**: it advises, and the authority matrix
> decides. This file is the record of what advises us, what used to, and why.

---

## 1. Lanes at a glance

| Lane | State | Since | Verdict / exact disqualifier |
|---|---|---|---|
| <LANE_NAME> | in effect | <YYYY_MM_DD> | <WHAT_IT_IS_GOOD_AT> |
| <LANE_NAME> | cancelled | <YYYY_MM_DD> | <THE_EXACT_DISQUALIFIER> |
| <LANE_NAME> | declined | <YYYY_MM_DD> | <WHY_IT_WAS_NEVER_ADOPTED> |

States: **in effect** (running and read), **cancelled** (was running, stopped),
**declined** (evaluated, never adopted), **removed** (config gone, owner-side
teardown confirmed).

**A disqualifier is exact or it is not a disqualifier.** "Did not work out" is
a mood. "Skips draft pull requests, and this repo reviews on drafts" is a fact
the next session can re-check in one minute and either confirm or overturn.

---

## 2. Per-lane block

Repeat one of these per lane, including the dead ones.

### <LANE_NAME>

- **State:** <IN_EFFECT_OR_CANCELLED>, since <YYYY_MM_DD>
- **Triggers:** <WHICH_EVENTS_FIRE_IT> (every push? open and ready only?)
- **Scope:** <WHICH_PATHS_IT_REVIEWS>
- **Instruction files:** <WHICH_FILES_IT_LOADS> (registered in the budget file)
- **Meter shape:** <THROTTLE_OR_HARD_STOP> - a throttle reopens after a window,
  a hard stop does not reopen until the period rolls. The two demand opposite
  reactions, and a lane whose shape is unrecorded gets waited on when it will
  never answer.
- **Reviews drafts:** <YES / NO> - per-lane pin (DEC-0013), default NO for a
  metered lane; changing it is a register edit with the meter facts beside it.
- **Caps and measured ceilings:** <MEASURED_LIMIT_AND_HEADROOM> - measured, not
  quoted from documentation. A config field that grows by policy will cross a
  vendor cap, and past the cap the tool can reject the whole config and keep
  running **on its defaults**, looking entirely normal.
- **Standing rules for this lane:** <WAIT_OR_SKIP_THRESHOLD>,
  <DRAFT_BEHAVIOR>, <WHICH_COMMANDS_ARE_NEVER_INVOKED>
- **Delivery format:** <ANCHORED_ITEMS / SUMMARY_ONLY> - require, in
  configuration where the tool supports it, that findings arrive as anchored,
  replyable, resolvable items; a lane that writes findings into author-owned
  surfaces (the pull-request body) is effectively silent (a measured 45-to-1
  inline gap, and twelve reviews discovered appended invisibly to a PR
  description).
- **Skip rules, classified:** each cost-saving exclusion is a
  <PRE_DISPATCH_GATE / IN_CONTEXT_INSTRUCTION> - only the gate saves money,
  nothing in the config file distinguishes them, and each gate is verified by
  watching one real change get skipped (FAST_TRACK.md).
- **Expected rejections:** <THE_LANE'S_KNOWN_NON-ANSWERS> - vendor
  unavailable, diff too large, already-reviewed. An expected rejection is
  the lane working, not a flake; re-run at most once.
- **Channel verification:** <CANARY_STATUS_AND_DATE> - the instrument that
  proves this lane's instruction files are READ, not merely parsed
  (`/reviewer-integration baseline`); until it fires, load-bearing rules stay
  duplicated in a verifiable channel with a stated sync rule.
- **Compute and billing:** <WHERE_ITS_RUNS_EXECUTE_AND_WHO_PAYS> - a hosted
  tool can be free on its own invoice and bill your CI minutes; a per-seat
  lane bills by the author of record, so automation-opened pull requests are
  authored by the covered identity (agent attribution goes in Co-Authored-By,
  never the author field).
- **Disjointness rationale:** <WHAT_THIS_LANE_CATCHES_THAT_THE_OTHERS_DON'T> -
  a second lane is bought for corroboration, and a lane overlapping an
  incumbent on the same axis is disqualified by redundancy even on a better
  score (TECH_EVALUATION.md section 3c).
- **Owner actions owed:** <WHAT_ONLY_THE_OWNER_CAN_DO> - uninstalling an app,
  changing a dashboard-side setting, adjusting branch protection. A
  cancellation an agent cannot finish is **tracked here**, never assumed done.

